    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "hopping on here, as I think I have a very similar problem.\r\n\r\nI'm trying to (re)install Numba to use tbb, preferably with pip on Ubuntu 18.04.2 LTS.\r\n\r\nWhat I've tried:\r\n\r\n1. pip3 install tbb==2020.0.133\r\n    pip3 install numba==0.53.1\r\n2. pip3 install tbb==2020.0.133\r\n    git clone git://github.com/numba/numba.git\r\n    git checkout release0.53\r\n    python setup.py install\r\n\r\nIn the first case, i get\r\n```\r\n__Threading Layer Information__\r\nTBB Threading Layer Available                 : False\r\n+--> Disabled due to Unknown import problem.\r\nOpenMP Threading Layer Available              : True\r\n+-->Vendor: GNU\r\nWorkqueue Threading Layer Available           : True\r\n+-->Workqueue imported successfully.\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn the second case, \r\n```bash\r\n06:39:59 \ud83e\udd16:numba$ python3 setup.py install\r\nTBB not found\r\nUsing OpenMP from: True\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\ncontext: I'm trying to serve a small dash app using Flask/wsgi/apache2, and it calls fit_transform() from sci-kit learn.  It runs fine locally, but when it's served, we suspect that the threading between Flask and numba is causing problems.\r\nhttps://github.com/lmcinnes/umap/issues/665",
