    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "@celinesin I think the issue you present is a variant on https://github.com/numba/numba/issues/6108, essentially, `pip` installed TBB sometimes cannot be found by Numba ([xref](https://github.com/numba/numba/issues/6108#issuecomment-675365997)) (though in the building from source case you'd also need a wheel equivalent to the conda `tbb-devel` package to get the TBB header files).\r\n\r\nGiven the context in https://github.com/lmcinnes/umap/issues/665, and that OpenMP is supported on your system, I'd try setting the threading layer to OpenMP ([docs](https://numba.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user/threading-layer.html#selecting-a-named-threading-layer)). Quickest way is via the environment variable `NUMBA_THREADING_LAYER=omp`.",
